---
/**
 * Privacy Policy — Brick Crack (App Store) / Brick Game (Google Play)
 *
 * Standalone page linked from the App Store Connect / Google Play listings
 * (the URL is registered in App Store Connect; keep it). Not linked from the
 * site nav. /brickgame-privacy redirects here (public/brickgame-privacy/).
 * A TR mirror lives at /tr/brickcrack-privacy so the header's language toggle
 * doesn't break for Turkish visitors who land here from a store listing.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { type Lang } from '@lib/i18n';

const lang: Lang = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
  lang={lang}
  title="Privacy Policy — Brick Crack (Brick Game)"
  description="Privacy policy for Brick Crack (App Store) / Brick Game (Google Play), the mobile block puzzle by Ekimoz Games."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <header class="mb-10 border-b border-border pb-8">
      <h1
        class="font-display font-medium text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-text-100 tracking-tight"
      >
        Privacy Policy — Brick Crack (Brick Game)
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-text-300 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest">
        Effective date: November 18, 2026
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-content space-y-4 text-text-200 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>Brick Crack</strong> (published as
        <em>Brick Game</em> on Google Play; together, "the App", "we", "our",
        or "us"), made by Yusuf Kaan Usta (Ekimoz Games), based in Türkiye, handles
        information when you use the App on iOS or Android. The rules for using the
        App are in the <a href="/brickcrack-terms/">Terms of Service</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The App has no account system of its own, no server and no user database.
        It does not ask you for a name, email address, phone number or any other
        personally identifying information. The only data that leaves your device
        goes to the third-party services described below (ads, Google Play Games on
        Android, and the app stores for purchases).
      </p>

      <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        The App saves the following on your device (Unity PlayerPrefs). It is not
        sent to us:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>your progress and scores;</li>
        <li>your settings (language, sound, theme);</li>
        <li>your Daily Challenge streak;</li>
        <li>flags that record which purchases you own.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The App shows banner, interstitial and rewarded ads through Unity LevelPlay
        (ironSource) and Unity Ads. Google AdMob is not used.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Ads are not personalized, for everyone.</strong> The App tells the
          ad SDKs that you have not consented to personalized advertising, so no
          separate consent screen is shown.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No tracking on iOS.</strong> The App does not ask for App
          Tracking Transparency permission and does not track you across other
          companies' apps or websites.
        </li>
        <li>
          Even for non-personalized ads, the ad SDKs may process device
          information (model, operating system, language, approximate region
          derived from your IP address), your interactions with ads, and on
          Android the advertising ID. They use this to show non-personalized ads,
          limit how often an ad appears, and prevent fraud.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Google Play Games Services (Android only)</h2>
      <p>
        On Android, the App signs you in to Google Play Games automatically and uses
        it for leaderboards, achievements and cloud save (Play Games Saved Games).
        The cloud save contains:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>the number of levels you have unlocked;</li>
        <li>your high scores (Classic, Advanced and Levels);</li>
        <li>the counter for the line-clearing achievement;</li>
        <li>whether you have seen the tutorial screens.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        On leaderboards, your Play Games name and avatar may be visible to other
        players, depending on your Play Games settings. This data is kept in your
        Google account and is handled under
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The iOS version does not use Game Center and has no leaderboards,
        achievements or cloud save.
      </p>

      <h2>In-app purchases</h2>
      <p>
        The App offers two one-time purchases: <strong>Premium</strong> (unlocks
        levels 16–115 and all themes, and removes ads) and
        <strong>Remove Ads</strong> (removes ads). Payment is handled by Google Play
        Billing and Apple In-App Purchase through Unity IAP. We never see your card
        number, billing address or store-account password; the App only receives
        the store's confirmation that a purchase was made, so it can unlock or
        restore it.
      </p>

      <h2>Notifications and sharing (Android)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Daily Challenge reminder.</strong> The App can show a local
          reminder notification at 8:00 PM for the Daily Challenge. It asks for
          notification permission once, after your first Daily Challenge win. The
          reminder is scheduled on your phone; there are no server push
          notifications. You can turn it off in your phone's settings at any time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sharing.</strong> You can share your Daily Challenge result as
          text through your phone's own share sheet. Nothing is sent to us.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Analytics and crash reports</h2>
      <p>
        The App contains no separate analytics or crash-reporting SDK. We only see
        the install and crash statistics that Google Play Console and App Store
        Connect provide in their own reports.
      </p>

      <h2>How the information is used</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To show ads inside the App and fund its development.</li>
        <li>
          To unlock the purchases you have made and let you restore them on a new
          device.
        </li>
        <li>
          On Android, to run leaderboards and achievements and to save your
          progress to your Google account.
        </li>
        <li>To fix bugs when the stores' crash reports show a real problem.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell or rent personal information, and we do not use App-related
        data for any purpose unrelated to operating Brick Crack.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        The third-party services the App relies on have their own privacy policies
        that govern how they handle the data they collect:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Unity Ads —
          <a href="https://unity.com/legal/game-player-and-app-user-privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            https://unity.com/legal/game-player-and-app-user-privacy-policy
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          Unity LevelPlay (ironSource) —
          <a href="https://www.is.com/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            https://www.is.com/privacy-policy/
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          Google Play / Google Play Billing / Google Play Games Services —
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            https://policies.google.com/privacy
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          Apple App Store / Apple In-App Purchase —
          <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Brick Crack is intended for a general audience and is not directed at
        children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal
        information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal
        information through the App, please contact us at the address below and we
        will work with our third-party providers to remove it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Notifications:</strong> turn off the Daily Challenge reminder in
          your phone's notification settings for the App.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Android advertising ID:</strong> Settings → Google → Ads lets you
          reset or delete your advertising ID.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>iOS tracking:</strong> Settings → Privacy &amp; Security →
          Tracking controls whether apps may ask to track you. The App does not ask
          in any case.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Local data:</strong> uninstalling the App deletes all the data it
          stored on your device.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Play Games data (Android):</strong> your cloud save and Play Games
          data stay in your Google account. You can delete them from the Google Play
          Games app or your Google account settings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Purchases</strong> stay linked to your store account and can be
          brought back with Restore Purchases (in the Premium panel and the pause
          menu).
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live (for example the European Union, United
        Kingdom, Türkiye, California, or Brazil), you may have rights to access,
        correct, delete, or restrict the processing of personal information about
        you, or to opt out of certain data uses.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          For data held by the ad services, Google or Apple, refer to their privacy
          policies linked above; they handle that data.
        </li>
        <li>To reach us directly, write to the contact address below.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We do not run our own server, so there is nothing for us to retain on our
        side. Data on your device stays there until you uninstall the App. On
        Android, the cloud save is kept in your Google account under Google's
        rules. The other third-party services listed above retain data according
        to their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy when the App's data practices change.
        The effective date at the top of this page reflects the last revision.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about this policy or about Brick Crack, please write to:
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Yusuf Kaan Usta</strong> (Ekimoz Games)<br />
        <a href="mailto:kaanekimoz@gmail.com">kaanekimoz@gmail.com</a><br />
        Türkiye
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
